PhotoCraft for HarmonyOS (照片工坊 / 雕光)
Copyright 2026 PhotoCraft for HarmonyOS contributors

This is an unofficial, non-commercial HarmonyOS port of the upstream
PhotoCraft editor. It is NOT maintained by, affiliated with, or endorsed by
the upstream project or ArtCraft.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Upstream software
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
This product contains a native engine compiled from the source of:

    PhotoCraft — https://github.com/storytold/photocraft
    Copyright Storytold / ArtCraft
    Licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0 (dual license), at the licensee's option.

The engine binary (`libphotocraft_native.so`, `aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos`)
was compiled from that source plus the HarmonyOS port. The port adds, and
does not otherwise rewrite, the following:

  - `apps/photocraft-ohos` — a NAPI host crate: render thread on an
    OHNativeWindow surface (wgpu, GLES/EGL backend), input and platform
    request queues, system CJK font registration.
  - `crates/ui-egui` — made buildable without `eframe`, so the host drives
    `run_ui` itself instead of `eframe` owning a window and event loop.
  - Platform service implementations (file open/save, external links) that
    forward to ArkTS instead of a desktop dialog.

Upstream's own `zh-hans` translation table is used as-is; no upstream
strings were modified for this port.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Fonts
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
No font is bundled or redistributed by this project.

Chinese glyphs are rendered with the device's system font, which the host
registers as the lowest-priority fallback family after probing:

    /system/fonts/HarmonyOS_Sans_SC.ttf
    /system/fonts/NotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc
    /system/fonts/NotoSansSC-Regular.otf

Those fonts are provided by HarmonyOS and remain under their own licenses
(HarmonyOS Sans is distributed with the system; Noto CJK is OFL 1.1).
This repository does not ship a copy of either.

(The 1.x WebAssembly build embedded a subset of Noto Sans SC. That build,
its font, and the OFL Reserved-Font-Name caveat that came with it are no
longer part of this project; the historical recipe is archived under
`tools/build_engine_zh/`.)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Third-party Rust crates inside the .so
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The compiled engine statically links a large dependency tree (wgpu, egui,
naga, image codecs, ...). All of them are permissively licensed (MIT,
Apache-2.0, BSD, Zlib); no GPL/AGPL code is included.

An exhaustive, machine-generated list cannot live in this repository because
the upstream Cargo workspace is neither vendored nor redistributed here. To
regenerate it, run on a machine that has the upstream source checked out:

    cargo about generate --output-file THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md

and place the result next to this file before publishing a release.
